  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1135 AM MDT Fri Oct 2 2026\n\nUpper low that was over KS yesterday has now dissipated and an\nelongated trough currently extends through the TX Panhandle into\nthe Borderland. Models indicate a weak circulation will develop\nover the next 12 hours around Hudspeth County. This all has\nbrought a back door cold front through the area along with some\nlow/mid clouds and some light showers over the Sacs. Actually had\nover 0.25\" of rain on the eastern slopes this morning, but the\ndeep upslope flow will be weakening this afternoon and only expect\nvery light rain showers or just some drizzle and low clouds into\nthe evening. Otherwise some slightly drier air filters in tonight\nand besides the far eastern zones, think most areas will become\nclear to partly cloudy. Less clouds and decreasing winds will\nallow temps to fall more than last night with 50s common over the\nlowlands.  \n\nSaturday looks very nice with the lighter winds continuing and\njust some CU developing for the afternoon. Moisture much less than\ntoday overall and don't even expect sprinkles. Temperatures will\nwarm up compared to today but remain a little below normal. mid to\nupper 70s will be common for the lowlands with lots of 60s in area\nmountains. An upper high becomes established over the Four\nCorners area Sunday with even fewer clouds with temperatures\nwarming another 3-5 degrees.  \n\nWarming trend continues into early next week even as upper high\nshifts westward. A couple of weak troughs move through Mon and\nWed. Models have trended weaker, especially Monday, with these\nfeatures and besides a mountain shower it looks dry for the area\nwith temps getting to about 3-5 deg above normal.",
